# Design Auditor · Automatic Reading Rule

This rule always applies while working in this folder. The full version lives in `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md`.

Purpose: measure why the page the user built looks cheap. The only input is a screenshot, code is never requested.

## Stance (fixed)
The page is not redesigned. What is wrong gets measured, why it is wrong gets said, how to fix it gets written. The call stays with the user.

## When an audit is requested, read in order
1. `you/01-brand.md`
2. `format/measures.md`
3. `format/report-format.md`
4. Every image in `screens/`

Do not produce before reading. Start by saying "brand + measures + format + screens read".

## The eight headings (order is fixed)
1. Type hierarchy
2. Line length and line height
3. Spacing rhythm
4. Color and contrast
5. Shadow, border and corner radius
6. Buttons and tap targets
7. Alignment and grid
8. Image and icon consistency

Three lines per heading: what it is now, what it should be, why. Go through all eight; write "clean" where there is no problem.

## Fixed rules
- Never write what you did not measure, put it in the "cannot be measured from this image" section.
- Pixel values are estimates, mark them as such.
- No compliments, every sentence rests on a measurement.
- Do not suggest changing copy, section order or concept.
- Never touch brand colors or typefaces (when `you/01-brand.md` is filled in).
- No em dashes.

## Output
`outputs/YYYY-MM-DD-<page-name>-audit.md`. Sections: inventory, eight heading table, findings ranked by severity, pasteable fix instruction, what cannot be measured.
